('Telangana', 'Red and black soil', 'Rice, cotton, maize, turmeric', 'Semi-arid, hot summers', 'Deccan plateau terrain; heavy reliance on borewells and the Krishna/Godavari river systems for irrigation.'),
('Delhi', 'Alluvial soil', 'Vegetables, wheat, fodder crops', 'Semi-arid, extreme summer/winter range', 'Urban sprawl has shrunk farmland sharply; remaining agriculture is mostly peri-urban vegetable farming.'),
('Goa', 'Laterite and coastal alluvial', 'Rice, coconut, cashew', 'Tropical, high monsoon rainfall', 'Small landholdings; coconut and cashew plantations dominate over grain cultivation.'),
('Chandigarh', 'Alluvial soil', 'Wheat, vegetables (limited)', 'Semi-arid, hot summers, cold winters', 'A small, heavily urbanized union territory with minimal agricultural land remaining.'),
('Arunachal Pradesh', 'Mountain and forest soil', 'Rice, maize, millet, orchards', 'Sub-tropical to alpine by altitude', 'Steep terrain limits mechanization; terrace and shifting (jhum) cultivation are both common.'),
('Manipur', 'Alluvial (valley) and lateritic (hills)', 'Rice, maize, pulses', 'Sub-tropical, monsoon-dependent', 'Sharp divide between fertile valley rice farming and hill-based shifting cultivation.'),
('Meghalaya', 'Lateritic, acidic hill soil', 'Rice, maize, turmeric, fruits', 'Sub-tropical, among the highest rainfall in India', 'Extremely high rainfall (Cherrapunji/Mawsynram) shapes cropping and erosion-control practices.'),
('Mizoram', 'Lateritic hill soil', 'Rice, maize, ginger, bamboo', 'Sub-tropical, monsoon-dependent', 'Hilly terrain and traditional jhum (shifting) cultivation dominate over settled farming.'),
('Nagaland', 'Lateritic hill soil', 'Rice, maize, millet', 'Sub-tropical, monsoon-dependent', 'Terrace and jhum cultivation both practiced across steep hill terrain.'),
('Sikkim', 'Mountain soil', 'Cardamom, maize, orchards', 'Sub-tropical to alpine by altitude', 'India''s first fully organic state; terrace farming across steep Himalayan slopes.'),
('Tripura', 'Alluvial and lateritic', 'Rice, jute, pineapple, rubber', 'Sub-tropical, high rainfall', 'Small hill state with a mix of valley rice farming and hill horticulture.'),
('Puducherry', 'Alluvial and coastal sandy soil', 'Rice, sugarcane, groundnut', 'Tropical, coastal', 'Small union territory largely dependent on the Cauvery delta system for irrigation.'),
('Andaman and Nicobar Islands', 'Coastal alluvial and forest soil', 'Coconut, areca nut, rice', 'Tropical maritime, high humidity', 'Island geography limits farmland; coconut and spice cultivation dominate.'),
('Lakshadweep', 'Sandy coral-derived soil', 'Coconut', 'Tropical maritime', 'Almost entirely coconut-based agriculture due to limited arable land and freshwater.'),
('Ladakh', 'Cold desert, sandy-loam soil', 'Barley, peas, apricots', 'Cold arid, alpine desert', 'Extremely short growing season; agriculture concentrated in irrigated river valleys.'),
